@*
    Every component in this assembly is implementation, not contract (docs/architecture/admin-dashboard-review.md,
    F-10): the Razor SDK emits each `.razor` file as a public class because it has no per-component
    accessibility to set, not because a host is meant to construct or extend one. This attribute hides
    every component from a consumer's IntelliSense and marks `Components.*` as free to change in any
    minor version — the seven types in the `MMLib.Alvo.Admin` namespace itself (`AlvoAdmin`,
    `AlvoAdminAssets`, `AlvoAdminOptions`, `AlvoAdminClaims`, `IAlvoAdminCallerResolver`, and the two
    `Add`/`Map` extension methods) are the actual contract, and none of them is a Razor component. No
    component here is a supported extension point today (F-11's host extension API is deliberately not
    built yet), so the attribute applies uniformly rather than selectively.
*@
@attribute [System.ComponentModel.EditorBrowsable(System.ComponentModel.EditorBrowsableState.Never)]
